+## Alerting and detection (on-call signals)
+
+Detection is the host assurance lanes in
+`scripts/assurance/assurance.sh`, driven from the host crontab
+(`*/5` quick, `17 5 * * *` daily; capacity/perf on their own cadence). Each run
+appends an immutable line to `/home/user/assurance/run_ledger.jsonl`
+(`run id, lane, due/start/end UTC, duration, exit, results, trigger, host`). A
+non-zero lane exit is an **operator alert**, not a build failure, and sends an
+ntfy notification to the `NTFY_TOPIC` in `/home/user/.env` (sole transport).
+
+| Signal | Threshold / rule | Exit | First action |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Container health | any `snowride-*` container `unhealthy`/`Exited` | 2 | `docker compose ... ps`; logs; restart the affected service |
+| TLS certificate | leaf `fullchain.cer` < 14 days | 3 | [CERT_TLS.md](CERT_TLS.md) |
+| Disk free | auto-reclaim (`reclaim-disk.sh`) under 3 GB; alert if still < 2 GB | 12 | free space; inspect `/home/user/assurance/reclaim.log` |
+| Daily: test suite | any failing test | 4 | logs; revert the implicated switch/image |
+| Daily: backup freshness | newest `/home/user/backups/*.dump` older than 26 h | 5 | [BACKUP_RESTORE.md](BACKUP_RESTORE.md) |
+| Daily: exception drift | open exception count increased vs. last run | 6 | `evidence/closeout/EXCEPTION_REGISTER.md` |
+| Daily: a11y / OSV scan / offsite ledger / license / expiry | lane non-zero | 7–11 | see [ASSURANCE.md](ASSURANCE.md) |
+| Capacity / SLO | p95 or error-rate breach (`capacity-regression.mjs`) | 13 | `scripts/capacity-regression.mjs` |
+| Performance | frame-budget regression > 1.2x | 14 | `scripts/frame-budget.mjs` |
+| Drill | forced failure (`ASSURANCE_DRILL=1`) | 90 | expected; proves detection → delivery |
+
+Read the failing ledger line and the evidence files it references before acting
+(`tail -1 /home/user/assurance/run_ledger.jsonl`). Never edit past ledger lines —
+append the resolution.
+
+## Escalation
+
+There is **no committed on-call rotation** (see [Known gaps](#known-gaps)); the
+single operator/owner is the escalation point. Keep the handoff explicit:
+
+1. **Acknowledge** the ntfy alert and open a timeline (UTC).
+2. **Triage** per this runbook. If a rollout is implicated, stabilise first —
+   revert the switch/image before diagnosing (steps 1–2 above).
+3. **Escalate to the owner/operator** if the outage is user-visible, not
+   understood, or not mitigated within the incident window; involve the owner
+   immediately for anything involving data loss, a security boundary, or
+   leaderboard integrity.
+4. **Resolve and record**: append an evidence entry (below) and reconcile the
+   follow-up register with the incident reference.
+
